{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, all three domains have the same family SCCS, a.298.1.1, because TAL effectors are repeat proteins and the classification follows the homologous repeat module and its shared left-handed alpha-alpha-superhelix architecture, not equality of whole-domain length. d2kq5a_ is PthA and is explicitly annotated as a single repeat (51 residues); d3v6pa_ is the 373-residue dHax3 repeat array; and d4cj9a_ is the 752-residue BurrH array. Thus, their large length differences primarily reflect different numbers of tandem small repeats and associated terminal regions. Their common lineage is class a (all-alpha), fold a.298, superfamily a.298.1 (TAL effector-like), and family a.298.1.1 (TAL effector). SCOPe flags d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ with repeat-number heterogeneity (“re”), expressly allowing members of this family to contain different numbers of the repeating unit. The family’s canonical representative repeat is d4cj9a_, chain A residues 259–292, but those coordinates apply only to that representative and must not be transferred as boundaries to d2kq5a_ or d3v6pa_. Family membership supports close evolutionary relatedness of the repeat units; it does not establish a one-to-one full-chain alignment, identical repeat count, identical DNA-target specificity or biological function, or interchangeable whole-array templates. Repeat-aware alignment and target-specific structural or functional evidence are required for those transfers.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"get_scop_service_info: /api/v1/, /api/v1/releases/current\",\"get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/homology, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/homology, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/homology\",\"get_scop_sequence: /api/v1/sequences/sids/d2kq5a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json, /api/v1/sequences/sids/d3v6pa_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json, /api/v1/sequences/sids/d4cj9a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\"]}]}"}}
